// The generated game, checked here rather than in the developer's project.
//
// `templates/` is the product — `src/` is only the machinery that copies it —
// so this is the config that guards the deliverable. It extends
// `templates/tsconfig.json`, the config that ships *inside* the generated
// project, so the options here cannot drift from the ones the developer will
// run: change theirs and this changes with it.
//
// Only `include` differs, because the paths in theirs are relative to their
// project root, plus `types/template-placeholders.d.ts` for the three
// identifiers a template still has holes for.
//
// The imports resolve because `@babylonjs/core` and `kei-transaction` are
// devDependencies of *this* package at the same ranges `templates/package.json`
// declares — `kei-transaction` at the exact range the scaffolder writes, since
// `src/index.ts` reads it from here. So the template is checked against the
// versions a developer installs, and an SDK release that breaks the emitted
// game breaks this build rather than their first `bun run dev`.
{
  "extends": "./templates/tsconfig.json",
  "include": [
    "templates/src",
    "templates/server",
    "templates/shared",
    "types/template-placeholders.d.ts"
  ]
}
